## Conclusion

This assessment demonstrates that injection vulnerabilities remain one of the most critical and prevalent risks in web application security. Both SQL Injection and Reflected XSS were successfully exploited on DVWA using straightforward, well-known payloads — highlighting how dangerous these flaws are when input is not properly validated or encoded.

The findings reinforce why **OWASP A03:2021 – Injection** consistently ranks among the top web security risks globally. Remediation through prepared statements, output encoding, and input validation effectively closes these attack vectors and should be implemented as standard practice in all web application development.

